l,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null]},\"interval\":10,\"files\":[],\"prof_output\":\"/var/folders/0g/8xjn9t110q58xrg1zwh192280000gq/T//RtmpZmE1yj/fileaf2324f86cce.prof\",\"highlight\":{\"output\":[\"^output\\\\$\"],\"gc\":[\"^<GC>$\"],\"stacktrace\":[\"^\\\\.\\\\.stacktraceo(n|ff)\\\\.\\\\.$\"]},\"split\":\"h\"}},\"evals\":[],\"jsHooks\":[]}</script>\n```\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\nIt is especially instructive to click on the _data_ tab and open up\nthe tree for `psolve` to see the sequence of calls and cumulative time\nused.\n\n## Directly Calling the Solver\n\nWe are mathematically certain that the above is convex and so we can\navoid the repeated DCP checks. The three steps are:\n\n**Step 1.** Extract the compiled problem data using `problem_data()`.\nThis returns the low-level solver data, the compilation chain, and\ninverse data needed to reconstruct the solution.\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nprob_data <- problem_data(prob, solver = \"CLARABEL\")\n```\n:::\n\n\n**Step 2.** Call the solver directly via `solve_via_data()` on the\ncompilation chain. This bypasses DCP verification entirely.\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nsolver_output <- solve_via_data(prob_data$chain, prob_data$data,\n                                warm_start = FALSE, verbose = FALSE,\n                                solver_opts = list())\n```\n:::\n\n\n**Step 3.** Unpack the solver results back into the problem's\nvariables using `problem_unpack_results()`. This reverses the\ncompilation chain and populates `value(beta)` etc.\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nproblem_unpack_results(prob, solver_output,\n                       prob_data$chain, prob_data$inverse_data)\n```\n:::\n\n\n## Profile the Direct Call\n\nWe can profile this direct call now.\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nprofvis({\n    beta <- Variable(m)\n    obj <- Minimize(0.5 * sum((y - beta)^2) + lambda * sum(pos(diff(beta))))\n    prob <- Problem(obj)\n    prob_data <- problem_data(prob, solver = \"CLARABEL\")\n    solver_output <- solve_via_data(prob_data$chain, prob_data$data,\n                                    warm_start = FALSE, verbose = FALSE,\n                                    solver_opts = list())\n    problem_unpack_results(prob, solver_output,\n                           prob_data$chain, prob_data$inverse_data)\n})\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"profvis html-widget html-fill-item\" id=\"htmlwidget-11cd5528a3a962c32537\" style=\"width:100%;height:600px;\"></div>\n<script type=\"application/json\" data-for=\"htmlwidget-11cd5528a3a962c32537\">{\"x\":{\"message\":{\"prof\":{\"time\":[1,1,1,1,1,1,1,1],\"depth\":[8,7,6,5,4,3,2,1],\"label\":[\"make_vec\",\"get_problem_matrix\",\"coeff_quad_form\",\"method(reduction_apply, CVXR::ConeMatrixStuffing)\",\"reduction_apply\",\".compile_and_apply\",\"method(problem_data, CVXR::Problem)\",\"problem_data\"],\"filenum\":[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null],\"linenum\":[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null],\"memalloc\":[71.12952423095703,71.12952423095703,71.12952423095703,71.12952423095703,71.12952423095703,71.12952423095703,71.12952423095703,71.12952423095703],\"meminc\":[0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0],\"filename\":[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null]},\"interval\":10,\"files\":[],\"prof_output\":\"/var/folders/0g/8xjn9t110q58xrg1zwh192280000gq/T//RtmpZmE1yj/fileaf235da57249.prof\",\"highlight\":{\"output\":[\"^output\\\\$\"],\"gc\":[\"^<GC>$\"],\"stacktrace\":[\"^\\\\.\\\\.stacktraceo(n|ff)\\\\.\\\\.$\"]},\"split\":\"h\"}},\"evals\":[],\"jsHooks\":[]}</script>\n```\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## Same Answer?\n\nOf course, we should also verify that the results obtained in both\ncases are the same.\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nidentical(betaHat, value(beta))\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n[1] TRUE\n```\n\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## Session Info\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\nR version 4.6.1 (2026-06-24)\nPlatform: aarch64-apple-darwin23\nRunning under: macOS Tahoe 26.6.2\n\nMatrix products: default\nBLAS:   /Library/Frameworks/R.framework/Versions/4.6/Resources/lib/libRblas.0.dylib \nLAPACK: /Library/Frameworks/R.framework/Versions/4.6/Resources/lib/libRlapack.dylib;  LAPACK version 3.12.1\n\nlocale:\n[1] en_US.UTF-8/en_US.UTF-8/en_US.UTF-8/C/en_US.UTF-8/en_US.UTF-8\n\ntime zone: America/Los_Angeles\ntzcode source: internal\n\nattached base packages:\n[1] stats     graphics  grDevices utils     datase